    basic: "Conserve your Tens and Aces for 'Multi-Leads'. If you lead two 10s at once, the opponent must produce two cards to beat them, which is statistically difficult.",
    intermediate: "Stock Management: Always keep a Trump card in your hand to defend against a 'Bura' declaration. If you are 'void' of trumps, you are a vulnerable target for multi-card leads.",
    advanced: "The 'Goat' Trap: If you see an opponent has no tricks by the halfway point, lead low non-scoring cards to prevent them from winning anything. If they end with zero tricks, they take double penalty points (The Full Goat).",
    tips: [
      {
        title: 'Tip',
        description: 'Diamonds are traditionally trumps in Kozel, though house rules may vary.',
      },
      {
        title: 'Tip',
        description: "If you have a 'Bura' (3 trumps), don't play it immediately. Wait until the opponent leads a high-scoring 10 or Ace to capture it.",
